    "text": "Let <math><mi>A</mi></math> be a matrix such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\" separators=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> is a scalar matrix and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>108</mn></math>. Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;equals :"
